# Wave W17-P (Route 118): ford sand — bank-road sand: pale river sand with a cool wet-sheen fleck in the tread, the road that runs the banks and meets the old planks at the crossing (design-authorised: a clear connected path of pale sand running end to end, Lilac to the rain climb; the ford planks themselves are the shipped boardwalk kind, byte-preserved by spec — this sand is the banks’ own, not the crossing’s). Split from Route 119’s darker puddle-polished gauge sand by value: the ford road still dries between rains.
